WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:21.700
Hi there! Who are you?

2
00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:25.083
I'm a red kangaroo.

3
00:00:25.084 --> 00:00:29.716
Red kangaroos are marsupials.

4
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:37.616
Female marsupials carry their babies in pouches.

5
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:40.585
Where do you live?

6
00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:45.283
Red kangaroos live in Australia.

7
00:00:45.284 --> 00:00:55.151
We like open grasslands and deserts.

8
00:00:55.152 --> 00:01:00.606
Oh! I see your baby!

9
00:01:00.607 --> 00:01:04.148
He's called a joey.

10
00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:09.016
Joeys sometimes come out to explore.

11
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:19.239
After ten months they leave the pouch forever.

12
00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.875
What do you eat?

13
00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:28.361
Red kangaroos eat grass and leaves.

14
00:01:28.362 --> 00:01:33.596
We can last for several days without water.

15
00:01:33.597 --> 00:01:38.577
Do kangaroos really box?

16
00:01:38.578 --> 00:01:44.281
Male kangaroos often fight with their front paws.

17
00:01:44.282 --> 00:01:50.318
They also kick with their back legs.

18
00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:56.909
Do you have any enemies?

19
00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:03.545
Wild dogs called dingoes hunt us.

20
00:02:03.546 --> 00:02:10.560
We stomp our feet when danger is near.

21
00:02:10.561 --> 00:02:16.963
Your feet are long!

22
00:02:16.964 --> 00:02:20.660
Our feet are very strong too.

23
00:02:20.661 --> 00:02:24.871
They help us jump far.

24
00:02:24.872 --> 00:02:33.856
Red kangaroos can jump up to 12 meters!

25
00:02:33.857 --> 00:02:37.252
Uh-oh. I see a dingo!

26
00:02:37.253 --> 00:02:42.205
Good day!

27
00:02:42.206 --> 00:02:49.042
Good-bye, Red Kangaroo!
